messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S07
Scenario title: Meeting Summary and Email Reporting
Initial workflow description:
After a meeting, the contents are summarized and shared by email with the relevant people.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or action signals that a meeting has ended and that the summarization process should begin — for example, the meeting room being released, a calendar event ending, or a manual action by the organizer?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How is the meeting summary currently created — does a person write it manually from memory or notes, or is any tool used to record, transcribe, or draft it automatically?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "How is the list of email recipients determined — is it always the set of meeting attendees, a predefined distribution list, or does someone manually decide who should receive the summary each time?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Before the summary email is sent, does anyone need to review or approve it, and if so, who is responsible for that step?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Beyond the summary text itself, are there required elements in the email such as a list of action items, owners, decisions made, or attached documents?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Is there a target or maximum time limit within which the summary email must be sent after the meeting ends, and are there any consequences if that deadline is missed?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Summarize meeting content and distribute decisions, owners, and deadlines to relevant stakeholders.",
  "actors": [
    "meeting participant",
    "minute taker",
    "decision owner",
    "recipient"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "calendar system",
    "meeting transcript or notes",
    "email client",
    "task tracker"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "meeting agenda",
    "meeting notes or transcript",
    "participant list",
    "action-item list"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "meeting summary email",
    "decision list",
    "action-item assignments",
    "task tracker updates"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect meeting notes or transcript",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Extract decisions and action items",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Confirm unclear items with decision owners",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Draft summary email",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Attach or link supporting materials",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Send email to relevant recipients",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Update task tracker if needed",
      "actor": "decision owner"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all action items assigned to owners?",
      "branches": [
        "assigned",
        "clarification needed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Does the meeting require task tracking?",
      "branches": [
        "tracker update needed",
        "email only"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing transcript",
    "unclear decision owner",
    "recipient list incomplete",
    "confidential content included"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Decision and action-item extraction can be supported by summarization models."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Email drafting can be template-based."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Task tracker updates can be generated from action-item tables."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: convey the same information as above, but do not reuse the
reference workflow's wording. Rephrase every activity, system, artifact, actor and condition in your own
words while preserving the meaning. Do not copy reference phrases verbatim.

